<title>UK: Shield rises after upbeat press comment.</title>
<headline>Shield rises after upbeat press comment.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Britain's Shield Diagnostics Group Plc rose in pre-market trading on Monday on the back of positive press comment.</p>
<p>Saturday's Daily Mail, a long-time backer of the stock, cited analysts as saying the company could eventually rise to between 20 and 25 stg per share if its heart attack diagnostic kit proved successful.</p>
<p>Shares in Shield, which touched a high of 928 pence earlier this year, were up 20 1/2 pence at 590 by 0720 GMT.</p>
</text>
